"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproduced in `4.8.dev`[6220ead], `4.7.stable`.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1088) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12700H (20 threads) - 15.69 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRelated:\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123139\n\nWhen typing `@rpc` in the script editor, all of the accepted values for the first 3 arguments are shown together, which is very confusing to look at.\n\nScreenshot:\n<img width=\"1391\" height=\"467\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/379c5525-db35-4c02-b578-9cd49e17fd69\" />\n\nWhile the order of `mode`, `sync`, and `transfer_mode` technically does not matter when parsed ([Godot Docs](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_%40gdscript.html#class-gdscript-annotation-rpc)), I would expect the autocomplete to follow the order of the parameters shown in the completion tooltip:\n1. `mode` = `\"any_peer\"`, `\"authority\"`\n2. `sync` = `\"call_remote\"`, `\"call_local\"`\n3. `transfer_mode` = `\"unreliable\"`, `\"unreliable_ordered\"`, `\"reliable\"`\n4. `transfer_channel` = (no autocomplete option)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Type `@rpc(` in a script, and wait for the autocomplete to show up.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other